Package: maknae
Version: 0.1.0-1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Alex Ackerman <darkhonor@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/darkhonor/maknae
Depends: libc6, systemd, apparmor, apparmor-utils
Description: trust-plane daemon and operator CLI for a local AI-agent platform
 Maknae is a security-first, local AI-agent platform. This package installs
 the privileged trust-plane daemon (maknaed) and the non-privileged operator
 CLI (maknae), a hardened systemd unit with TPM2-sealed credential loading
 (LoadCredentialEncrypted), an AppArmor confinement profile, and the shipped
 DAC authorization policy — for deployment on hardened Debian systems.
 .
 A fresh install is not runnable until `sudo maknae enroll` provisions the
 daemon credential and the operator principal; the shipped authz.yaml uses
 `~` patterns and fail-closes until enrollment writes the principal. The
 daemon MUST be enrolled before it is started (install -> enroll -> start).
